    {
      "id": 129076,
      "name": "Killswitch",
      "username": "Killswitch",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/{size}/2116_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-23T14:13:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I would say that between an action and an ongoing effect, ongoing effects should take precidence. I would say his DR is \"ongoing.\" Any card text that prompts an action to occur immediately (\"At the start/end of the turn...\" \"Put ___ into play...\" \"Deal H targets X damage...\"). If it just says to decrease all damage, it's not telling you to necessarily do anything at the moment, so there's no order of operation. Rather, it's an \"ongoing\" action.</p><p>I don't really have any rulings to back this up, but I'm pretty sure that's how I would always play it.<br>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:03:56.853Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 12069,
      "topic_slug": "damage-reduction-and-enters-play",
