      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>I would say that between an action and an ongoing effect, ongoing effects should take precidence. I would say his DR is &quot;ongoing.&quot; Any card text that prompts an action to occur immediately (&quot;At the start/end of the turn...&quot; &quot;Put ___ into play...&quot; &quot;Deal H targets X damage...&quot;). If it just says to decrease all damage, it&#39;s not telling you to necessarily do anything at the moment, so there&#39;s no order of operation. Rather, it&#39;s an &quot;ongoing&quot; action.</p><p>I don&#39;t really have any rulings to back this up, but I&#39;m pretty sure that&#39;s how I would always play it.<br />&nbsp;</p>",
